<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexandros Papagos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1883–1955</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexandros Papagos was a Greek field marshal and politician. As commander-in-chief he led the Greek army that drove back the Italian invasion of 1940–1941, and in 1949 he directed the final defeat of the communists in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-civil-war">Greek Civil War</a>. He then founded the Greek Rally party, won the 1952 elections and was Prime Minister until his death in 1955.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexandros-papagos.jpg" alt="Alexandros Papagos" width="320" height="469" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer, taken as part of the series Photographs of Marshall Plan Programs, Exhibits, and Personnel, 194... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexandros_Papagos_as_PM.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
